  "details": "Creators upload stuff for users on their behalf, but it requires their login credentials which isn't the greatest for obvious security reasons.\n\nMy suggestion is to let a user generate a one-time login code in the VRCSDK in Unity, and on the website, to give to someone else that will log into their account with only the limited permissions to upload a new avatar or world, and/or update an existing one.  No returned worlds or avatars in the contents panel, no logging to VRChat itself, just a brief secure authorized session to upload an avatar or world.  If they need, and lack, an existing avatar's ID, the user can provide it themselves.\n\nThis means the workflow on a custom avatar becomes just giving the creator the login code, good for (let's say) an hour or two, and wait for upload knowing their account's still secure.",
